      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some NIMBY concerns are valid, there are legitimate technical and economic arguments against high-density zoning. For instance, increased density can lead to strain on local infrastructure, such as water and sewage systems, and may require significant investments in transportation and public services. Additionally, high-density development can also lead to increased energy consumption, noise pollution, and strain on local resources. These concerns are often overlooked in favor of the benefits of high-density development, but they are legitimate and should be taken into consideration.",
      "source": "target",
